{"duration_api_ms":191742,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"398e0c9f-5d4a-485a-bb2e-3c3917915ef7","total_cost_usd":0.24918600000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16343,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18381,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":12821},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16343,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":18381,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16343},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":18381,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16343,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.24918600000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":12821,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The front is a one-dimensional curve. It comes from designs at D~3.384, B=1.2, cone=70 with flight_path_angle_deg swept from -1.5 to -3.57 (flux 227k-275k W/m2, bondline T 418-391 K). Three caps pin it. Peak g is about 1.7/deg of steepness and reaches the 12 limit at gamma~-3.57. Heatshield mass margin scales as D^2 and reaches zero at D~3.38524. B and cone are at the surrogate-hull and variable bounds. Hypervolume gains have fallen to ~1e-4 per round.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-25994855d0b4 (D=3.3852, gamma=-3.57): g margin 4e-5 and mass margin 2.7e-5, so both caps are active at once.\",\"C-92f6aed905e3 to C-eed229743768: T falls ~10-16 K/deg and flux rises ~20-24k W/m2/deg along gamma at fixed geometry. Spacing gaps remain at gamma -3.0 to -3.3, -2.1 to -2.3 and -1.5 to -1.65.\",\"C-363a563b3536 (D=3.3, gamma=-3.58) has flux 285k and T 392.5, worse than the D=3.384 points. Smaller D therefore does not help.\",\"C-02209f2ea644 (B=1.15) has a lower mass margin than B=1.2, so lower B is worse. C-3d41ce848a30 and C-05beb8f06d5f (B=1.21 and 1.205 at cone 70) fail the surrogate hull, so the B bound lies between 1.2 and 1.205.\",\"Round-7 hypervolume 0.355471 to 0.355514 shows the front is saturated.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Flux and T fall with ballistic coefficient and nose radius, which favours large D, B and cone. The mass fraction (~D^2, slightly worse at lower B) caps D. Peak g depends almost only on gamma and caps steepness. This is my reading of the data, plus the general Rn^-0.5 heating scaling from prior knowledge. Little remains except filling gamma gaps and adding the last 0.0012 m of D, which trims flux by ~150 W/m2 and T by ~0.02 K. Two probes test whether B can rise slightly above 1.2 at cone 70, which would relieve the mass cap.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The interpolated predictions are linear and could be off by a few hundred W/m2 or ~0.3 K. The g boundary at gamma=-3.5702 is within ~1e-4 of the limit. The hull probes at B=1.201 and 1.202 may fail as a no-geometry extrapolation. I have no evidence of any un-tried region that beats this corner.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-4da368065e68\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the largest front gap (gamma -3.0 to -3.3) at the D cap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3852,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.05},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":262035,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.47,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a gap in the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4da368065e68\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap in gamma -3.0 to -3.3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3852,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":263240,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.93,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a gap in the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4da368065e68\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap in gamma -3.0 to -3.3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3852,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.15},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":264450,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.39,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a gap in the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e9fb95df2518\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap in gamma -3.0 to -3.3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3852,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":265650,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.86,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a gap in the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e9fb95df2518\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap in gamma -3.0 to -3.3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3852,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":266860,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.32,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a gap in the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4682430c8b55\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -3.3 and -3.45.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3852,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.375},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269860,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.02,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a gap in the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4682430c8b55\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -3.3 and -3.45.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3852,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":270460,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.77,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a gap in the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6ffb6b7edb43\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap near the g cap with D at the mass cap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3852,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.53},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273585,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.48,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a gap in the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-eed229743768\",\"rationale\":\"Push D to its cap at gamma -3.55.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3852,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274060,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.38,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Marginally better than the neighbouring D=3.384 points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-25994855d0b4\",\"rationale\":\"Approach the g cap at gamma -3.565.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.565},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274425,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.13,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Approaches the g cap, where g is predicted ~11.99.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-25994855d0b4\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the exact g boundary (g predicted ~11.9999).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5702},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274555,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.09,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests how steep gamma can go at the g cap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-92f6ae